This Python snippet is a clean and effective way to calculate both the active sampling duration and the total elapsed wall-clock time for data collected in alternating bursts and pauses.

What the Code Does
Active Sampling Time: Computes the total time the sensor or device was actively recording by dividing the total number of samples (len(data)) by the sampling rate (16 samples/second).

Estimated Elapsed Time: Accounts for both the active recording periods and the pauses between them. It assumes each increment in the BurstCounter represents a 1-minute burst followed by a 1-minute pause (120 seconds total per step), plus the exact duration of the samples recorded in the final burst.

